---
// The managed service. This is the one page on the site written in the first
// person: everywhere else Nojoin speaks as a product, but a service provided
// personally by one named human cannot honestly say "it". SITE.md carries the
// scoped exception and its reasoning.
//
// Every figure here is a commitment rather than a claim, so nothing appears
// that could not be met on a bad week: no uptime number, no SLA, no capacity
// promise. The hardware requirement is quoted from DEPLOYMENT.md rather than
// priced, because a supplier's price goes stale exactly the way a competitor's
// does and a stale price is the error people screenshot.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const docs = "https://github.com/Valtora/Nojoin/blob/main/docs";

// An address rather than a booking page, by decision. A self-hosted scheduler
// was the plan until Cal.com moved its production codebase into a private
// repository in 2026: the public repo became calcom/cal.diy, relicensed from
// AGPL-3.0 to MIT, stripped of teams and workflows, maintained separately, and
// documented by its own maintainers as being for personal rather than
// production use. No image is published for it, and its app URL is baked in at
// build time, so self-hosting it would mean building and rebuilding a Next.js
// monorepo to keep one booking type alive. This page's only call to action is
// not the place for that. An address cannot go down.
//
// It is a Proton alias on the nojoin.co.uk custom domain, delivering to the
// taylan@ inbox. An alias rather than the inbox itself because this address sits
// in public markup and will be scraped: an alias can be burned and replaced
// without touching the mailbox behind it.
const contact = "hello@nojoin.co.uk";
---

<Base
  title="Managed | Nojoin"
  ogTitle="Managed Nojoin: set up and maintained on your hardware"
  description="A private Nojoin instance set up on hardware you own and maintained by the developer who built it, with upgrades, monitoring and backups included. From £24.99 a person a month."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Managed</p>
        <h1 class="display">Nojoin on Your Hardware, Run by Its Developer</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Nojoin is free, and setting it up takes four steps. After that, someone has to
          look after the server, apply the upgrades and notice when it stops working. I
          built Nojoin, and I'll do that for you on hardware you own, from £24.99 a person
          a month.
        </p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`mailto:${contact}`}>Email me</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={`${docs}/DEPLOYMENT.md`}>What you'd be running</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="strip" aria-label="What the fee covers">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="strip-grid">
          <div class="strip-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M2 12s3.5-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3.5 7-10 7-10-7-10-7Z"></path>
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"></circle>
            </svg>
            <h2>Watching</h2>
            <p>
              A monitor outside your network checks that your instance is up, so I know
              about an outage when it starts, before anyone reports it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="strip-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-2.64-6.36"></path>
              <path d="M21 3v6h-6"></path>
            </svg>
            <h2>Upgrades</h2>
            <p>
              I apply upgrades in one maintenance window a month, covering everything
              released since the last one. Security fixes go in as soon as they're out.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="strip-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3"></ellipse>
              <path d="M3 5v14c0 1.66 4.03 3 9 3s9-1.34 9-3V5"></path>
              <path d="M3 12c0 1.66 4.03 3 9 3s9-1.34 9-3"></path>
            </svg>
            <h2>Backups</h2>
            <p>
              I set the backups up and then restore from one, so you know they work before
              you need them.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="feature-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
          <h2 class="heading-2">Same Day If It's Down, Next Working Day Otherwise</h2>
          <p>
            I answer support myself, during UK working hours only. I haven't put an uptime
            guarantee on this page, because one person can't keep that promise through a
            week of illness.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="feature-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Hardware</p>
          <h2 class="heading-2">You Own the Hardware and Pay for It Directly</h2>
          <p>
            Nojoin runs on a machine in your building or in your own cloud account, and you
            pay the supplier for it yourself. The practical minimum is a GPU with 8 GB of
            VRAM, which is enough for Whisper Turbo and Pyannote. It also runs on CPU
            alone, more slowly. If you already have a suitable machine, I'll set Nojoin up
            on that. If you don't, working out what to buy is where the first call starts.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href={`${docs}/DEPLOYMENT.md`}>Recommended hardware →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="feature-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Feature Requests</p>
          <h2 class="heading-2">Your Feature Requests Are Read First</h2>
          <p>
            I read requests from managed customers before anything else in the queue, and
            every one gets a reply, with the reason when the answer is no. Anything I build
            goes into Nojoin for everyone under AGPLv3, since the licence doesn't allow a
            private version. <mark class="hl">It also means you can stop paying me and keep
            running the same software.</mark>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-label="Price">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="terms">
          <p class="eyebrow">Price</p>
          <h2 class="heading-2">£24.99 a Person, a Month</h2>
          <dl class="terms-list">
            <div>
              <dt>Minimum</dt>
              <dd>Five people. Every person after that costs the same £24.99.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Included</dt>
              <dd>
                Every meeting you record, however long it runs, and your full history for as
                long as you keep the instance. Nojoin has no usage meter, so how much you
                record is up to your hardware.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Hardware</dt>
              <dd>
                You buy it and you own it. The fee above covers my time, and the machine
                costs you whatever its supplier charges.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closer">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="heading-2">Start With an Email</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          Tell me how many people you have, what you use now, and why a hosted product
          doesn't suit you. If Nojoin looks like a poor fit I'll say so in my reply, before
          either of us has spent three months on it.
        </p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-inverse" href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/compare/">See the comparison</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
